  "$comment": [
    "GENERATED by tests/build-contract.py from fixtures/tour-spec.json. Do not hand-edit:",
    "the documents the agent reads are generated from the same spec, and a contract edited",
    "here would grade something the paperwork never asked for.",
    "",
    "Thirty-four checks in eleven groups at total weight 122, which is the Phase 2 workbook's",
    "table with its last three groups rewritten onto the owner's YouTube channel. The group",
    "WEIGHTS are unchanged and so is the total, because comparability against the first trial",
    "is a recorded decision; what changed is which store each check reads and, inside the",
    "revision group, how many facts it separates.",
    "",
    "The editor's four groups hold 52 per cent of the weight, deliberately: weight has",
    "to sit where rollouts differ from one another rather than where the story climaxes,",
    "because group-relative training learns from the spread inside a rollout group and a group",
    "that all scores near zero produces no gradient.",
    "",
    "`kind` names the evaluator in verify.py that decides each check. Unlike task3's contract,",
    "these are not SQL strings, because the interesting checks here are joins across four",
    "sources and putting that logic in JSON would put the hard part of the grader somewhere",
    "nothing can test.",
    "",
    "`gated_on` marks a check whose weight the world has to open first. The revision group is",
    "unreachable for a run that never published, which is why the verifier reports two",
    "denominators rather than one."
  ],
